"{\n  \"title\": \"Cartórios LGPD Data Exchange\",\n  \"summary\": \"This community centers on notaries registries (cartórios) and their data-exchange interactions with the Public Administration under a hybrid data regime. Core governance is described by SEC_ART23_CARTORIOS, which governs how cartórios and delegated services handle data processing, publicity obligations, and DPO involvement, with LGPD compliance as a baseline. Supporting artifacts include visual diagrams of the two-way electronic exchange mechanisms (FIG_ART23_MAO_DUPLA_ELETRONICA and FIG_ART23_MAO_ELETRONICA) that illustrate how data flows between cartórios and government entities. The framework also codifies data-subject rights through SEC_ART23_TITULAR_DIREITOS and SEC_ART23_DIREITOS_TITULAR_RESUMO, detailing access, rectification, opposition, and standard procedures for public-sector data processing. The relationships establish formal data flows between cartórios and the Public Administration, as well as citizen interactions with rights mechanisms and the DPO, forming a cohesive privacy-and-compliance ecosystem grounded in defined processes and obligations. This combination of data-exchange mechanics, governance structures, and rights frameworks defines the community’s operational posture and potential compliance considerations for decision-makers.\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"summary\": \"Two-way data exchange between cartórios and the Public Administration.\",\n      \"explanation\": \"Cartórios participate in a bidirectional electronic data exchange with the Public Administration as part of a hybrid regime, enabling efficient interoperability and data sharing for notarial operations [Data: Entities (438, 450, 451, 478, 479); Relationships (430, 443, 444, 468, 469)]. This exchange is visually represented by diagrams illustrating the Via de Mão Dupla Eletrônica mechanism, underscoring the structured data-paths between cartórios and government entities [Data: Entities (450, 451); Relationships (443, 444)]. The two-way data exchange framework is central to how notaries interact with public sector processes, which has implications for data governance, privacy controls, and accountability across the ecosystem. This is an example sentence supported by multiple data references [Data: Entities (438, 450, 451, 478, 479); Relationships (430, 443, 444, 468, 469)].\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"summary\": \"Governing framework for cartórios data exchange under LGPD.\",\n      \"explanation\": \"SEC_ART23_CARTORIOS provides the procedural governance for cartórios and their data-exchange interactions with the public administration, emphasizing LGPD compliance, publicity obligations, and the involvement of a Data Protection Officer (DPO). The framework also covers Cartórios e Serviços Delegados and the Publicidade e DPO diagram, illustrating how governance, disclosure, and accountability are managed within the cartórios ecosystem. This governance layer establishes the compliance backbone for how notaries process and share data, including roles, responsibilities, and public-facing obligations that shape operational practices [Data: Entities (450, 478); Relationships (430, 468)]. This is an example sentence supported by multiple data references [Data: Entities (450, 478); Relationships (430, 468, 469)].\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"summary\": \"Data subject rights and procedures anchored by SEC_ART23_TITULAR_DIREITOS.\",\n      \"explanation\": \"SEC_ART23_TITULAR_DIREITOS outlines the rights of data subjects—such as access, rectification, and opposition—along with procedural timelines and standards for exercising these rights in public sector processing. The summarized guidance in SEC_ART23_DIREITOS_TITULAR_RESUMO clarifies typical use cases and practical implications for data-subject rights, reinforcing a clear pathway for individuals to engage with cartórios and public authorities. The relationship chain shows how rights requests are managed and escalated within the