a: Entities (450, 451); Relationships (443, 444)]. This is an example sentence supported by multiple data references [Data: Entities (450, 451); Relationships (443, 444)].\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"summary\": \"Overall risk and compliance posture within the cartório data-exchange ecosystem.\",\n      \"explanation\": \"The integrated LGPD-compliance orientation, DPO involvement, and explicit data-subject rights processes collectively shape a moderate-to-elevated risk profile for privacy and regulatory compliance. While the LGPD framework provides clear obligations and accountability mechanisms, the reliance on two-way data exchange with the Public Administration and public-facing rights procedures creates multiple touchpoints where data governance controls must be consistently applied and audited. Ongoing monitoring of data flows, access controls, and rights-management procedures is implied by the combination of LGPD-centric provisions (via SEC_ART23_CARTORIOS) and rights-specific sections (SEC_ART23_TITULAR_DIREITOS and SEC_ART23_DIREITOS_TITULAR_RESUMO) [Data: Entities (450, 478, 479); Relationships (430, 468, 469)]. This is an example sentence supported by multiple data references [Data: Entities (450, 478, 479); Relationships (430, 468, 469)].\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"rating\": 6.0,\n  \"rating_explanation\": \"Moderate-to-high due to the formal data-exchange framework between notaries and the Public Administration coupled with mandated privacy governance and rights procedures.\"\n}"}, "metrics": {"attempted_request_count": 1, "successful_response_count": 0, "failed_response_count": 0, "responses_with_tokens": 1, "prompt_tokens": 2797, "completion_tokens": 6313, "total_tokens": 9110, "compute_duration_seconds": 28.27120304107666, "streaming_responses": 0, "retries": 0, "requests_with_retries": 0}}}